    p The role of nuclear mechanics, shape, and integrity in confined cell migration and how the cytoskeleton participates in these processes has begun to be elucidated. The nucleus and DNA can be damaged by mechanical stress , suggesting that cells have nucleo-protective mechanisms that operate during confined migration.

